    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0079" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg69"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 803.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 6, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I acknowledge the receipt of your despatch
                    of December 11, No. 556, together with its accompaniment, namely, your note
                    addressed to Earl Russell, with proofs in the case of the Canton <hi
                        rendition="#italic">alias</hi> the Pampero, a piratical steamer, which is
                    being built at Glasgow. Later advices by telegram state that her Majesty’s
                    government has forbidden the departure of that hostile craft. It is to be hoped
                    that this information is correct.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
